(Title) Tj
T*
(Clinical Outcomes of a Smartphone-Delivered Behavioral Flexibility Intervention for) Tj
T*
(Anxiety Disorders) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(A 10-week randomized controlled trial examined whether an evidence-based psychological) Tj
T*
(app, delivered via smartphone and integrated into standard care, reduced anxiety severity) Tj
T*
(in 96 adults \(mean age 38 years\) with generalized anxiety disorder. Half received the) Tj
T*
(application alongside standard counseling and support; the other half received standard) Tj
T*
(support alone. At 10 weeks, the application group demonstrated greater reduction in) Tj
T*
(anxiety ratings \(mean difference -2.1 points on the 21-point scale, p = 0.003\) compared to) Tj
T*
(controls. Secondary outcomes including worry measures and depressive symptoms showed) Tj
T*
(improvements across all measures in the intervention group, with effect sizes ranging from) Tj
T*
(small to moderate. Approximately 68% of users engaged with the prescribed frequency at the) Tj
T*
(intervention midpoint, declining slightly to 62% by week 10. Improvements were largely) Tj
T*
(sustained through the 15-week follow-up. Patient satisfaction with the digital tool was) Tj
T*
(high, with 79% reporting it was helpful or very helpful. Results suggest smartphone-) Tj
T*
(delivered psychological interventions can produce clinically meaningful anxiety reduction) Tj
T*
(when integrated into routine care.) Tj
